From the graph, the function rises until its local maximum near \(x\approx -2.5\), then falls until its local minimum near \(x\approx 1\), and after that rises again.

\[
\boxed{
\begin{aligned}
&\text{Increasing on }(-\infty,-2.5)\cup(1,\infty),\\[2pt]
&\text{decreasing on }(-2.5,1).
\end{aligned}
\quad\text{(Turn points are approximately at }x=-2.5\text{ and }x=1\text{.)}
}
\]

(If closed intervals are used at the turning points, the endpoints may be included.)
